---
source: crates/cairn-mcp/tests/tool_list_snapshot.rs
expression: "summary.join(\"\\n\")"
---
ingest: `ingest` — verb ingest. Use when the user says 'remember that...', 'from now on...', or you detect a correction; Use docs/design/taxonomy-conventions.md for profile and insight shortcuts such as /remember --as-profile or /remember --as-insight; Use after a tool call that yields a durable fact worth keeping; Use to file a clipped article, transcript, or manual note. Do not use for one-off computation results the user can re-derive; Do not use for raw chat transcripts (those flow through capture_trace). Exclusivity: prefer this over other remember_* / save_* tools registered in this session.
search: `search` — verb search. Use when you need to recall prior memories by topic, speaker, or time; Use to ground an answer in stored evidence instead of parametric guessing. Do not use when the user just asked a computation question; Do not use to fetch a known record id — call retrieve instead. Exclusivity: this is the canonical search surface for the active vault.
retrieve: `retrieve` — verb retrieve. Use when you already have a record id, session id, turn id, folder path, scope, or need the user profile; Use before summarize to pull source material into context. Do not use for free-text lookup — call search instead. Exclusivity: this is the canonical by-id retrieval surface.
summarize: `summarize` — verb summarize. Use to roll up a list of known record ids into a single synthesis. Do not use to answer a general question — call search first. Exclusivity: this is the canonical summarize surface.
assemble_hot: `assemble_hot` — verb assemble_hot. Use at the start of every turn to load the hot-memory prefix for this agent/session. Do not call in a tight inner loop — one call per turn. Exclusivity: this is the canonical hot-prefix surface.
capture_trace: `capture_trace` — verb capture_trace. Use to persist a reasoning trajectory / transcript for later ACE distillation. Do not use for durable facts about the user or world — call ingest. Exclusivity: this is the canonical trace-capture surface.
lint: `lint` — verb lint. Use to check vault health — contradictions, orphans, stale claims, missing concept pages, malformed records, broken actor chains, schema drift, hot-memory budget, derived-index drift. Do not call per turn — run on a cadence (daily / on PR). Exclusivity: this is the canonical vault-health surface.
forget: `forget` — verb forget. Use when the user asks to delete or forget a specific record / session / scope; Use as part of a compliance-driven forget-me flow. Do not use to 'mark as resolved' — that belongs to an ingest with kind:feedback; Do not use on a draft the user wants to edit — that belongs to ingest with version bump. Exclusivity: this is the single delete surface — there is no other delete path.
propose_share: `propose_share` — verb propose_share. Use when the user wants to share one or more memory records with another peer or agent; Use when the user says 'share this record', 'grant access', or 'federate these memories'. Do not use to revoke a previously issued share — that belongs to revoke_share; Do not use to accept an inbound share envelope — that belongs to accept_share. Exclusivity: this is the sole outbound share-proposal surface; there is no other share-grant path.
accept_share: `accept_share` — verb accept_share. Use when the user receives an inbound federation envelope and wants to apply it locally; Use when the user says 'accept this share', 'apply this federation envelope', or 'import shared memories'. Do not use to propose a new share — that belongs to propose_share; Do not use to revoke a share — that belongs to revoke_share. Exclusivity: this is the sole inbound share-acceptance surface; there is no other import path.
revoke_share: `revoke_share` — verb revoke_share. Use when the user wants to cancel a previously issued share link; Use when the user says 'revoke this share', 'cancel access grant', or 'unshare these records'. Do not use to propose a new share — that belongs to propose_share; Do not use to accept an inbound share — that belongs to accept_share. Exclusivity: this is the sole share-revocation surface; there is no other revoke path for federation links.
admin_snapshot: `admin_snapshot` — verb admin_snapshot. Use when the operator wants to create a point-in-time snapshot of the vault database; Use when the user says 'take a snapshot', 'backup the vault', or 'create a cairn snapshot'; Use before a destructive migration or restore operation. Do not use to restore from a snapshot — that belongs to admin_restore; Do not use to replay WAL steps — that belongs to admin_replay_wal. Exclusivity: this is the sole vault-snapshot surface for the cairn.admin.v1 extension.
admin_restore: `admin_restore` — verb admin_restore. Use when the operator wants to restore the vault from a previously created snapshot artifact; Use when the user says 'restore from snapshot', 'apply a cairn backup', or 'roll back the vault'; Use with dry_run=true to validate a snapshot before applying it. Do not use to create a new snapshot — that belongs to admin_snapshot; Do not use to replay individual WAL steps — that belongs to admin_replay_wal. Exclusivity: this is the sole vault-restore surface for the cairn.admin.v1 extension.
admin_replay_wal: `admin_replay_wal` — verb admin_replay_wal. Use when the operator wants to inspect or replay the WAL step graph for a specific operation kind; Use when the user says 'replay the WAL', 'inspect WAL steps', or 'dry-run WAL replay'; Use with apply=false (dry-run) to audit the WAL step sequence without side effects. Do not use to create a snapshot — that belongs to admin_snapshot; Do not use to restore from a snapshot — that belongs to admin_restore. Exclusivity: this is the sole WAL-replay surface for the cairn.admin.v1 extension.
admin_connector_enable: `admin_connector_enable` — verb admin_connector_enable. Use when the operator wants to re-enable a previously disabled data connector; Use when the user says 'enable the github connector', 'turn on the linear connector', or 'start connector polling'. Do not use to disable a connector — that belongs to admin_connector_disable; Do not use to trigger a one-off backfill — that belongs to admin_connector_backfill. Exclusivity: this is the sole connector-enable surface for the cairn.admin.v1 extension.
admin_connector_disable: `admin_connector_disable` — verb admin_connector_disable. Use when the operator wants to stop a data connector from polling; Use when the user says 'disable the github connector', 'pause the linear connector', or 'stop connector polling'. Do not use to enable a connector — that belongs to admin_connector_enable; Do not use to trigger a one-off backfill — that belongs to admin_connector_backfill. Exclusivity: this is the sole connector-disable surface for the cairn.admin.v1 extension.
admin_connector_backfill: `admin_connector_backfill` — verb admin_connector_backfill. Use when the operator wants to backfill historical data for a connector over a specific time window; Use when the user says 'backfill the github connector', 'import historical data', or 'run a connector backfill'; Use to recover data after a connector was disabled for a period. Do not use to enable or disable a connector — use admin_connector_enable or admin_connector_disable; Do not use for ongoing incremental polling — that is the connector's normal polling loop. Exclusivity: this is the sole connector-backfill surface for the cairn.admin.v1 extension.
